1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:04,025
Your phone says twenty percent. Then it
dies in a minute.

2
00:00:05,575 --> 00:00:09,809
You blame a dying cell. The problem is a
lying gauge.

3
00:00:10,779 --> 00:00:14,949
The gauge reads voltage, and voltage sags
under load.

4
00:00:15,919 --> 00:00:17,119
That is the trick.

5
00:00:18,669 --> 00:00:22,912
The gauge reads twenty percent. The cell
is nearly empty.

6
00:00:24,462 --> 00:00:26,737
A cheap cable drops the voltage.

7
00:00:27,707 --> 00:00:30,810
Cold weather slows the reaction inside the
cell.

8
00:00:31,780 --> 00:00:34,342
A three year old cell simply holds less.

9
00:00:35,892 --> 00:00:39,365
Forty five percent of the error is voltage
sag.

10
00:00:40,335 --> 00:00:41,730
Twenty is cold.

11
00:00:42,700 --> 00:00:44,233
Thirty five is age.

12
00:00:45,783 --> 00:00:46,908
Run one check.

13
00:00:47,878 --> 00:00:49,562
It is called battery health.

14
00:00:51,112 --> 00:00:56,499
Replace the cable if the sag is sudden.
Replace the cell if the cell is old.

15
00:00:58,049 --> 00:01:00,455
Gauge, cable, cell.

16
00:01:01,425 --> 00:01:02,910
Check them in that order.

17
00:01:04,460 --> 00:01:08,418
Check the cable first. It is the cheapest
of the three.
